<DocsLayout
  title="Setup & browser support"
  description="What you need before you start building visuals in Astrofox."
>
  <p>
    Astrofox runs in the browser. There is no installer, but the browser and
    machine you use make a real difference to playback smoothness and export
    reliability.
  </p>

  <h2>Recommended browser</h2>
  <p>
    Recent Chromium-based browsers such as Chrome, Edge, and Brave give the
    best support for WebGL, Web Audio, file saving, and video recording.
    Firefox and Safari can work, but some file APIs and export behaviors may be
    more limited.
  </p>

  <h2>Recommended hardware</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A modern laptop or desktop from the last few years.</li>
    <li>A GPU that can handle WebGL smoothly.</li>
    <li>Enough RAM to keep your browser, media files, and other tabs open without swapping.</li>
    <li>Headphones or speakers if you are tuning visuals against detailed frequency ranges.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Before your first session</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Open <a href="https://app.astrofox.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">app.astrofox.io</a>.</li>
    <li>Allow audio or microphone access if you plan to use live input.</li>
    <li>Load a short audio file first so you can judge preview performance quickly.</li>
    <li>Start with a simple display and one reactor before layering on effects.</li>
  </ol>

  <h2>When performance is tight</h2>
  <p>
    If the stage feels sluggish, work at a smaller canvas size, reduce effect
    count, and close other GPU-heavy tabs. See <a href="/docs/performance">Performance tuning</a>
    for the detailed checklist.
  </p>

  <h2>Browser permissions</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Microphone</strong> is required for live mic input.</li>
    <li><strong>MIDI</strong> access is required if you want to drive visuals from a controller.</li>
    <li><strong>File access</strong> is used when loading assets and choosing an export destination.</li>
  </ul>

  <div class="callout">
    Astrofox is easiest to learn in a desktop Chromium browser with a short
    audio track and a 720p canvas.
  </div>
</DocsLayout>
